  "result": "NRS_484B_633_2 is finished: the gate returned **OK** on its first run (6 witnesses, 11 names, no composed rules), so 5 of the 6 gate runs are unused.\n\n- **Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_633_2.lean`):\n  - **Subject:** a vehicle, as the aggregate `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle` defines it.\n  - **When the rule applies:** the vehicle is on a bridge or other elevated structure that lies on a highway. At the same moment, a speed limit sign of kind `structure_maximum` governs a lane or other travel region the vehicle is in.\n  - **The duty:** for every such sign, the vehicle's speed must be at or below the value the sign states.\n\n  I added no narrowings, because the record left nothing open.\n- **Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_633_2.lean`): the five planned scenarios (forbid, permit, idle, blind, branch_1). I added a sixth, `branch_2`: a signposted bridge that lies on no highway, expected not applicable. Without it, no witness tested the \"lies on a highway\" condition.\n- **Blocked command:** before the gate run, I sent one stray command that wasn't the gate command. The permission system denied it, nothing ran, and it used none of the gate budget.\n\n`task_result.md` in the working directory has the details.",
